WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/telemetry/components/SignalSelector.tsx — a CONTROLLED multi-select specialised for signal
  names (a `ComboboxMulti` wrapper). Regions + branches reproduced:
    • label <span> : `${t('Signals')} (${value.length} / ${max})`  — and `(${value.length})` when `max` is null,
                     and the explicit `labelOverride` when provided (uppercase / tracking-wider / text-muted).
    • HelpTooltip  : shown when `showLayerHelp` (default true) — i18nKey "help.signal.layers" (+ the long default)
                     and ariaLabel "help.signal.layers.aria".
    • ComboboxMulti: `label={t('Signals')}` (hidden), placeholder `t('Search signals…')`, a search icon, each
                     option rendered in a monospaced font (`renderOption` → font-mono), `maxItems={cap}`.
    • cap          : `cap = max ?? +Infinity`; `max` DEFAULTS to 5; `null` ⇒ no cap. `onChange` is
                     `onChange(Number.isFinite(cap) ? next.slice(0, cap) : next)` — i.e. the new value is clamped
                     to the first `cap` entries before bubbling to the parent.
  Data sources (per the prompt): `useTranslation` only — there is no data hook in the leaf component. The
  available-signal list (web `options`) is the data the embedding page supplies (production:
  /signals/{vehicleID}/available); the native surface binds that list through a P1/S8 state-holder seam so the
  HIG loading/empty/error/stale/offline states can be layered around the always-present selector.

