PARITY MAPPING (web → Apple platform tokens; no Tailwind ported)
  ComboboxMulti (@/components/forms) → TSComboboxMulti (Sources/Components/Forms/Inputs.swift); each signal →
                                       TSComboOption(title:searchText:); collapsed prompt = t('Search signals…').
  HelpTooltip   (@/components/ui)    → TSHelpTooltip (Sources/Components/UI/Overlays.swift); help text via the
                                       facade; the inner "?" a11y label is OVERRIDDEN with help.signal.layers.aria
                                       so the web ariaLabel parity holds while the button stays actionable.
  label span (text-xs uppercase      → Text(verbatim:) · Font.TS.label · .textCase(.uppercase) ·
    tracking-wider text-muted)         .tracking(TSTypeMetrics.labelTracking) · Color.TS.textMuted.
  renderOption font-mono             → the SELECTED signals are surfaced as monospaced chips (Font .monospaced)
                                       in the feature view (the atomic TSComboboxMulti owns its option-row font and
                                       is out of this surface's scope — P4 component-library bundle); the code-like
                                       signal-name intent is preserved in the region this surface owns.
  cap (max ?? ∞, slice(0,cap))       → SignalSelectorProjection.applyChange: removals always applied; new picks
                                       appended (options-order, then sorted out-of-list extras) only while under the
                                       cap → at the cap a new pick is rejected, exactly like slice(0,cap). nil = ∞.
  i18n                               → every string from the P1/S10 facade; zero English literals in code paths.
  a11y                               → label carries "Signals, N of M selected"; help button has its own aria;
                                       chips region reads "Selected signals: …"; decorative glyphs hidden; Dynamic
                                       Type via tokens; reduce-motion respected (TSFadeIn).
  telemetry                          → view.opened surface="SignalSelector" via the model on first start (P1/S11).

STATES (every state renders — no hidden surfaces; each has a preview + test)
  loading  : available-signal list fetching → skeleton hint under the always-present field.       (preview+phase test)
  empty    : list resolved with zero signals → friendly "no signals available" hint, never blank. (preview+phase test)
  error    : list fetch failed → inline QueryError-equivalent with a Retry affordance.             (preview+phase test)
  stale    : freshness past window → amber "may be stale" banner + ONE guarded auto-refresh.       (preview+model test)
  offline  : no connectivity → muted "showing last loaded signals" banner, cached list, NO refresh.(preview+model test)
  content  : signals available → bar speaks for itself (label + field + chips + optional cap hint). (preview+tests)

